  "scope": "poolwatch-v2",
  "stamp": "20260929_094815_standing_acceptance_standard_poolwatch_v2_addendum_2",
  "standard_id": "standing_acceptance_standard_poolwatch_v2",
  "title": "Poolwatch v2 standing standard - addendum 2: prices come from Poolwatch v2's own collector (every universe pool, every day)",
  "what_changes": {
    "daily_fix": "A day's price is its DAILY FIX: the last sample whose block timestamp is in [09:00:00, 09:30:00) UTC that day. A sample whose block is more than 180 s from the wall clock is discarded (stale node). A day with no fix is a missing day - it is never filled from Poolwatch or any other source.",
    "freeze": "The 09:30 UTC freeze (addendum 1) uses TODAY's fix as the entry price; a pool without one is skipped that day, disclosed in the run log.",
    "outcome": "breach = 1 if ANY daily fix in (freeze_day, freeze_day + 14 days] is outside the frozen band; fewer than 13 fixes in the window makes the row INCOMPLETE. Same daily sampling as before (intraday excursions still invisible; a breach can only be missed, never invented).",
    "price_source": "From freeze day 2026-09-30, every price the standard uses - the entry price a band is centred on, and each outcome day's price - is the pool's OWN on-chain rate read by poolwatch_v2/pw_collector.py: Uniswap v3 slot0.sqrtPriceX96 converted with both tokens' decimals to the asset's price in its dollar-stable quote leg, read through Multicall3 every 10 minutes. The asset/quote orientation of every pool is fixed in pw_price_meta.json (sha256 below).",
    "row_marker": "Rows frozen under this addendum carry snap_date = 'pw-collector fix @ <block time>' instead of a Poolwatch snapshot date, so every row names its own price source."
  },
  "what_does_not_change": "Universe (and its sha256), models PW-B1 / PW-B1-own / PW-P1 and model_version pw-v2.0.0 (their inputs - Market Weather candles and Poolwatch's own daily history for the own/pooled models - are unchanged), widths, tiers, the judging rule, cadence, the freeze instant (09:30 UTC, addendum 1) and the confident-calls trigger (family addendum 1). Rows frozen BEFORE 2026-09-30 keep the sealed Poolwatch-snapshot rule for their entry AND their outcome, even where their window runs past the effective day; their missing days stay missing.",
  "why": "Poolwatch's daily snapshot records only the top pools on each network, so universe pools fall out on some days (1-6 of 41 per day since 09-26; XAUt/USDT three days running, PAXG/USDC two). A pool missing on the freeze day gets no forecast; a pool missing on 2+ days of its window makes that forecast INCOMPLETE (13 of 14 days are required). The forecast object promises every universe pool, so the price source must cover every universe pool."
}